TABLE OF CONTENTS

btprofile/BTProfileBind
btprofile/BTProfileUnbind
btprofile/BTProfileBind                                btprofile/BTProfileBind

   NAME
	BTProfileBind -- A service offered: true if the driver takes it - it has filled a unit, `binding.unit` saying which, and keeps `binding` until BTProfileUnbind - false if it declines and the next driver is asked.

   SYNOPSIS
	    bool BTProfileBind(*bluetooth.BTBinding binding)

   BEHAVIOR
	Called on the library's binder process, which serves nothing else
	meanwhile: the driver may call the library - read the service's record,
	add listeners, open channels - and wait for it.
btprofile/BTProfileUnbind                            btprofile/BTProfileUnbind

   NAME
	BTProfileUnbind -- The service is taken back - its controller gone, or its bond ended (BTPU_FORGET in `flags`, for the driver to tell the device first, while the link is there): its channels closed, its unit left without it, `binding` no longer the driver's.

   SYNOPSIS
	    void BTProfileUnbind(*bluetooth.BTBinding binding, u32 flags)

   BEHAVIOR
	Called on the binder process.
